  "text_md": "215. Moment of inertia of a right circular cylinder about a line tangent to its base.\n216. Moment of inertia of a segment cut from a sphere by a plane, about a diameter parallel to that plane.\n217. Center of gravity of a right circular cone whose density varies as the distance from the center of the base.\n218. Volume bounded by the xy-plane, the cylinder x+ V 2 = 2 ax and the cone z= x 2 + y 1 -\n219. Find the attraction of a unifprm wire of length I and mass M on a particle of unit mass at distance c from the wire in the perpendicular at one end.\n220. Find the attraction of a right circular cylinder on a particle at\n7. the middle of its base.\n221. Show that the attraction of a homogeneous shell bounded by two concentric spherical surfaces on a particle in the enclosed space is zero.\n\n## CHAPTER X\n\nSolve the following differential equations:\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n223. sin x sin y dx + cos x cos ydy = 0.\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n230. (sin x -\\-y) dy -\\(y cos x - x 2 ) dx = 0.\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n234. x dy - y dx = Vx 2 -\\- y 2 dx.\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n236. xdy - ydx = x ^x 2 -f y 2 dx.\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n239. (3 ?/ 2 + 3 xy + x 2 ) dx = (x 2 + 2 xy) dy.\n\n240. (1 + x 2 ) dy + (xy - x 2 ) dx = 0.",
